# vc-x1 config file

Configure the work-repo of a dual repo system. The other repo, we call the agent-repo, is
also a markdown configuration file typically named .vc-config.md.

The code blocks in these config files are in toml format and these blocks are logically
concatenated in the order written here and those become the information used for configuring
the system. The [vc-config.md](vc-config.md) contains the documentation for the
various toml tables used for configuration and it is also used during compilation to define
the valid contents of this file.

The file [vc-config-test.md](vc-config-test.md) is a simple version of this file.
(I think we might rename the file vc-config-test.md to vc-config-model.md and it should
also contain every table and key/value pair showing typical or default values, my thoughts)

The two repos
- work [[1]]
- bot [[2]]
```toml
[repos]
work = "."
agent = ".claude"
```

The agent-file family this repo belongs to: its member name and the sibling repos it answers to
- member [[3]]
- template [[4]]
- messages [[5]]
```toml
[family]
member = "zc-ring-x1"
template = "../vc-x1-template"
messages = "../vc-x1-messages"
```

The validation commands, each element one invocation, run in order by `vc-x1 validate`
- full [[6]]
- fast [[7]]
```toml
[validate]
full = [
  "cargo fmt",
  "cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings",
  "cargo test",
  "cargo install --path . --locked",
]
fast = ["cargo test --bins"]
```

# References

[1]: vc-config.md#reposwork
[2]: vc-config.md#reposbot
----
[package]
name = "zc-ring-x1"
# Version-of-record (see agent-data/versioning.md): advanced through
# the cycle's X.Y.Z-N phases; the -N rides in the semver
# prerelease slot.
version = "0.15.4"
edition = "2024"
rust-version = "1.96"
license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
description = "Zero-copy no_std SPSC + MPSC ring buffer experiment"

# Dev artifact name (agent-data/versioning.md): the package and
# demo binary carry -dev while a cycle runs, the library keeps
# its plain name so no `use` line changes. Land restores them.
[lib]
name = "zc_ring_x1"

[[bin]]
name = "zc-ring-x1-demo"
path = "src/bin/zc-ring-x1-demo.rs"

[dependencies]
zerocopy = { version = "0.8", default-features = false, features = ["derive"] }

# Demo-binary only: thread pinning for the pinned ring runs.
[target.'cfg(target_os = "linux")'.dependencies]
libc = "0.2"

# Local measurement crates (probes, runner, cells+bins); dev
# tooling only — not dependencies of the library. See
# tp_matrix/ for the installable tp-cell / tp-matrix binaries.
[workspace]
members = ["tprobe", "tp_runner", "tp_matrix"]

